IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`

-- coa26-ch2d.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 2 (Individuals and firms), ss 1225 to 1225G: enforcement against recognised
-- supervisory bodies and recognised qualifying bodies (directions, compliance orders, financial penalties, appeals, recovery).
-- Lines 17281-17385 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. These provisions address the Secretary of State, the court and the bodies, so they are
-- encoded for what they decide; the seat layer asks only what they mean to a person (see coa26-seat.l4).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, each such branch
-- with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment). A bare "must" that is not done, a "where" or
-- "if" that fails, and an "unless" that is met are all JUST FALSE here (rulings of 2026-11-05; decided case by case, see the fork register).
-- Periods counted in months use `Date`, which rolls an impossible day forward; a month-end start date is therefore a fork.

§§ `Enforcement`

-- ---- s 1225: Enforcement: general ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17283 | (1) This section applies if at any time it appears to the Secretary of State—
-- src:17284 | (a) in the case of a recognised supervisory body, that any requirement of Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10 is not satisfied,
-- src:17285 | (b) in the case of a recognised professional qualification offered by a recognised qualifying body, that any requirement of Part 2 of Schedule 11 is not satisfied, ...
-- src:17286 | (c) that a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of this Part (other than an obligation to pay a financial penalty under section 1225D) or
-- src:17287 | (d) that a recognised supervisory body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
@ref s 1225(1) When the section applies (src:17283-17287)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body does not satisfy a requirement of Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised professional qualification offered by a recognised qualifying body does not satisfy a requirement of Part 2 of Schedule 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of Part 42 (other than an obligation to pay a financial penalty under section 1225D)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF     `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body does not satisfy a requirement of Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10`
        OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised professional qualification offered by a recognised qualifying body does not satisfy a requirement of Part 2 of Schedule 11`
        OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of Part 42 (other than an obligation to pay a financial penalty under section 1225D)`
        OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that a recognised supervisory body has not complied with an obligation imposed on it by or by virtue of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if at any time it appears to the Secretary of State—"

-- src:17288 | (2) The Secretary of State may do any one or more of the following—
-- src:17289 | (a) give a direction to the body under section 1225A;
-- src:17290 | (b) make an application to the court in respect of the body under section 1225C;
-- src:17291 | (c) impose a financial penalty on the body under section 1225D.
@ref s 1225(2) What the Secretary of State may do (src:17288-17291)
GIVEN `section 1225 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225(2) the Secretary of State may do any one or more of the things in paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
    -- (a) give a direction under section 1225A, (b) apply to the court under section 1225C, (c) impose a financial penalty under section 1225D
    CONSIDER `section 1225 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) is the Secretary of State's power under a section that applies only on the facts in subsection (1); other powers are not decided here
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether it appears to the Secretary of State is not known

-- src:17292 | (3) Subsection (2) is without prejudice to the powers of the Secretary of State under paragraph 3 of Schedule 10 and paragraph 3 of Schedule 11 (revocation of recognition orders) or the powers of the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
@ref s 1225(3) Powers not prejudiced (src:17292)
GIVEN `the power is a power of the Secretary of State under paragraph 3 of Schedule 10 or paragraph 3 of Schedule 11 (revocation of recognition orders), or a power of the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225(3) subsection (2) is without prejudice to the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is a power of the Secretary of State under paragraph 3 of Schedule 10 or paragraph 3 of Schedule 11 (revocation of recognition orders), or a power of the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) is without prejudice to the powers of the Secretary of State under paragraph 3 of Schedule 10 and paragraph 3 of Schedule 11 ... or the powers of the competent authority"

-- ---- s 1225A: Directions: general ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17294 | (1) A direction under this section is one directing a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will—
-- src:17295 | (a) secure that the requirement in question is satisfied or the obligation in question is complied with, or
-- src:17296 | (b) mitigate the effect, or prevent the recurrence, of the failure to satisfy the requirement or comply with the obligation.
@ref s 1225A(1) A direction under this section (src:17294-17296)
GIVEN `the direction directs a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will secure that the requirement in question is satisfied or the obligation in question is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction directs a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will mitigate the effect, or prevent the recurrence, of the failure to satisfy the requirement or comply with the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225A(1) the direction is a direction under section 1225A` MEANS
    IF     `the direction directs a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will secure that the requirement in question is satisfied or the obligation in question is complied with`
        OR `the direction directs a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will mitigate the effect, or prevent the recurrence, of the failure to satisfy the requirement or comply with the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction under this section is one directing a body to take such steps as the Secretary of State considers will— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:17298 | (a) may only require a body to take steps which it has power to take;
@ref s 1225A(2)(a) Only steps the body has power to take (src:17298)
GIVEN `the body has power to take the step` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225A(2)(a) the direction may require the body to take the step` MEANS
    IF `the body has power to take the step`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction under this section— (a) may only require a body to take steps which it has power to take"

-- src:17299 | (b) may require a body to refrain from taking a particular course of action.
@ref s 1225A(2)(b) Refraining from a course of action (src:17299)
GIVEN `the direction requires the body to refrain from taking a particular course of action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225A(2)(b) the direction may require the body to refrain from taking a particular course of action` MEANS
    IF `the direction requires the body to refrain from taking a particular course of action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) may require a body to refrain from taking a particular course of action"

-- src:17300 | (3) The power to give a direction under this section is subject to any provision made by or under any other enactment.
@ref s 1225A(3) Subject to other enactments (src:17300)
GIVEN `another enactment makes provision limiting the power to give the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225A(3) the power to give the direction is subject to the provision of another enactment` MEANS
    IF `another enactment makes provision limiting the power to give the direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any provision made by or under any other enactment" (the provisions of other enactments are outside the sources)

-- src:17301 | (4) The Secretary of State may take such steps as the Secretary of State considers appropriate to monitor the extent to which a direction under this section is being, or has been, complied with.
@ref s 1225A(4) Monitoring compliance (src:17301)
GIVEN `the step is one the Secretary of State considers appropriate to monitor the extent to which a direction is being, or has been, complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225A(4) the Secretary of State may take the step` MEANS
    IF `the step is one the Secretary of State considers appropriate to monitor the extent to which a direction is being, or has been, complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such steps as the Secretary of State considers appropriate to monitor"

-- ---- s 1225B: Directions: supplementary ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- A "must" that is not done is JUST FALSE here: the function asks whether the Secretary of State has done what the subsection requires.

-- src:17303 | (1) Before giving a direction to a body under section 1225A, the Secretary of State must give the body a notice (a “notice of proposed direction”) accompanied by a copy of the proposed direction.
@ref s 1225B(1) Notice of proposed direction (src:17303)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State gave the body a notice of proposed direction accompanied by a copy of the proposed direction before giving the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(1) the notice of proposed direction was given before the direction` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State gave the body a notice of proposed direction accompanied by a copy of the proposed direction before giving the direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before giving a direction to a body under section 1225A, the Secretary of State must give the body a notice"

-- src:17304 | (2) A notice of proposed direction must—
-- src:17305 | (a) state that the Secretary of State proposes to give the body a direction in the form of the accompanying draft,
-- src:17306 | (b) identify the requirement or obligation in question and state why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with,
-- src:17307 | (c) specify a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposal.
@ref s 1225B(2) Content of the notice of proposed direction (src:17304-17307)
GIVEN `the notice states that the Secretary of State proposes to give the body a direction in the form of the accompanying draft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice identifies the requirement or obligation in question and states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(2) the notice of proposed direction has the required content` MEANS
    IF     `the notice states that the Secretary of State proposes to give the body a direction in the form of the accompanying draft`
       AND `the notice identifies the requirement or obligation in question and states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with`
       AND `the notice specifies a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice of proposed direction must— (a) state ... (b) identify ... (c) specify a period"

-- src:17308 | (3) The period specified under subsection (2)(c)—
-- src:17309 | (a) must begin with the date on which the notice of proposed direction is given to the body, and
-- src:17310 | (b) must not be less than 14 days.
@ref s 1225B(3) The period for representations (src:17308-17310)
GIVEN `the period begins with the date on which the notice of proposed direction is given to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the length of the period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(3) the period specified under subsection (2)(c) is valid` MEANS
    IF `the period begins with the date on which the notice of proposed direction is given to the body` AND `the length of the period in days` AT LEAST 14
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period specified under subsection (2)(c)— (a) must begin with the date on which the notice of proposed direction is given to the body, and (b) must not be less than 14 days."

-- src:17311 | (4) Written representations made by the body within the period specified under subsection (2)(c) must be considered by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1225B(4) Representations must be considered (src:17311)
GIVEN `the body made written representations within the period specified under subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considered them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(4) the Secretary of State has complied with the duty to consider the representations` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body made written representations within the period specified under subsection (2)(c)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Written representations made by the body within the period specified under subsection (2)(c) must be considered"
    ELSE IF `the Secretary of State considered them`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Written representations made by the body within the period specified under subsection (2)(c) must be considered by the Secretary of State."

-- src:17312 | (5) After considering any such representations or, in their absence, on the expiry of the period specified under subsection (2)(c), the Secretary of State must decide whether to give the body the proposed direction.
@ref s 1225B(5) The decision whether to give the direction (src:17312)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has considered any representations or, in their absence, the period specified under subsection (2)(c) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(5) the Secretary of State must now decide whether to give the proposed direction` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has considered any representations or, in their absence, the period specified under subsection (2)(c) has expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After considering any such representations or, in their absence, on the expiry of the period specified under subsection (2)(c), the Secretary of State must decide" (a time fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:17313 | (6) The Secretary of State must give notice of the decision (a “direction decision notice”) to the body.
@ref s 1225B(6) Notice of the decision (src:17313)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decided whether to give the proposed direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(6) the Secretary of State has given notice of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decided whether to give the proposed direction` AND `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must give notice of the decision (a “direction decision notice”) to the body."

-- src:17314 | (7) Where the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction, the direction decision notice must—
-- src:17315 | (a) contain the direction,
-- src:17316 | (b) state the time at which the direction is to take effect, and
-- src:17317 | (c) specify the Secretary of State's reasons for the decision to give the direction.
@ref s 1225B(7) Content of the direction decision notice (src:17314-17317)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice contains the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the time at which the direction is to take effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the Secretary of State's reasons for the decision to give the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(7) the direction decision notice has the required content` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction`
    THEN (IF `the notice contains the direction` AND `the notice states the time at which the direction is to take effect` AND `the notice specifies the Secretary of State's reasons for the decision to give the direction`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the direction decision notice must— (a) contain the direction, (b) state the time at which the direction is to take effect, and (c) specify the Secretary of State's reasons"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17318 | (8) Where the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction, the Secretary of State must publish the direction decision notice in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the direction to the attention of persons likely to be affected.
@ref s 1225B(8) Publication of the direction decision notice (src:17318)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State published the direction decision notice in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the direction to the attention of persons likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(8) the Secretary of State has published the direction decision notice` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction` AND `the Secretary of State published the direction decision notice in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the direction to the attention of persons likely to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Secretary of State decides to give the proposed direction, the Secretary of State must publish the direction decision notice"

-- src:17319 | (9) The Secretary of State may revoke a direction given to a body under section 1225A and, where doing so, must—
-- src:17320 | (a) give the body notice of the revocation, and
-- src:17321 | (b) publish the notice in the same manner as the direction decision notice was published.
@ref s 1225B(9) Revocation of a direction (src:17319-17321)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State revokes a direction given to a body under section 1225A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State published the notice in the same manner as the direction decision notice was published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225B(9) the revocation of the direction complies with subsection (9)` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State revokes a direction given to a body under section 1225A`
    THEN (IF `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the revocation` AND `the Secretary of State published the notice in the same manner as the direction decision notice was published`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where doing so, must— (a) give the body notice of the revocation, and (b) publish the notice in the same manner as the direction decision notice was published"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may revoke a direction given to a body under section 1225A and, where doing so, must"

-- ---- s 1225C: Compliance orders ------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1225C(3) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1225C(3) the High Court`
    `s 1225C(3) the Court of Session`

-- src:17327 | (3) In this section, “ the court ” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 1225C(3) "the court" (src:17327)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1225C(3) court`
`s 1225C(3) the court is` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
    THEN `s 1225C(3) the Court of Session`
    ELSE `s 1225C(3) the High Court`

-- src:17323 | (1) If on an application under this section in respect of a body, the court decides that a requirement is not satisfied or an obligation has not been complied with, the court may, subject to subsection (2), order the body to take such steps as it considers will secure that the requirement is satisfied or the obligation is complied with.
@ref s 1225C(1) The court may order the body to take steps (src:17323)
GIVEN `an application is made under section 1225C in respect of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides that a requirement is not satisfied or an obligation has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225C(1) the court may order the body to take such steps as it considers will secure that the requirement is satisfied or the obligation is complied with` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under section 1225C in respect of the body` AND `the court decides that a requirement is not satisfied or an obligation has not been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section in respect of a body, the court decides that a requirement is not satisfied or an obligation has not been complied with, the court may"

-- src:17324 | (2) Where the obligation is an obligation to comply with a direction under section 1225A, the court may not order compliance with the direction unless it also decides that—
-- src:17325 | (a) the requirement in respect of which the direction was given is not satisfied, or
-- src:17326 | (b) the obligation in respect of which the direction was given has not been complied with.
@ref s 1225C(2) Orders to comply with a direction (src:17324-17326)
GIVEN `the obligation is an obligation to comply with a direction under section 1225A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court also decides that the requirement in respect of which the direction was given is not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court also decides that the obligation in respect of which the direction was given has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225C(2) the court may order compliance with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the obligation is an obligation to comply with a direction under section 1225A`
    THEN (IF `the court also decides that the requirement in respect of which the direction was given is not satisfied` OR `the court also decides that the obligation in respect of which the direction was given has not been complied with`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may not order compliance with the direction unless it also decides that—"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the obligation is an obligation to comply with a direction under section 1225A"

-- ---- s 1225D: Financial penalties: general -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17330 | (2) In deciding what amount is appropriate the Secretary of State—
-- src:17331 | (a) must have regard to the nature of the requirement which is not satisfied or the obligation which has not been complied with; and
-- src:17332 | (b) must not take into account the Secretary of State's costs in discharging functions under this Part.
@ref s 1225D(2) How the amount is decided (src:17330-17332)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has regard to the nature of the requirement which is not satisfied or the obligation which has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State takes into account the Secretary of State's costs in discharging functions under Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225D(2) the Secretary of State has decided the amount in accordance with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has regard to the nature of the requirement which is not satisfied or the obligation which has not been complied with` AND (NOT `the Secretary of State takes into account the Secretary of State's costs in discharging functions under Part 42`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In deciding what amount is appropriate the Secretary of State— (a) must have regard to ...; and (b) must not take into account the Secretary of State's costs in discharging functions under this Part."

-- src:17329 | (1) A financial penalty imposed on a body under this section is a financial penalty of such amount as the Secretary of State considers appropriate, subject to subsection (2).
@ref s 1225D(1) The amount of the penalty (src:17329)
GIVEN `the amount is such as the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was decided in accordance with subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225D(1) the amount is a lawful amount of financial penalty` MEANS
    -- "of such amount as the Secretary of State considers appropriate, subject to subsection (2)"
    IF `the amount is such as the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
    THEN `the amount was decided in accordance with subsection (2)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A financial penalty imposed on a body under this section is a financial penalty of such amount as the Secretary of State considers appropriate"

-- src:17333 | (3) A financial penalty under this section is payable to the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1225D(3) Payable to the Secretary of State (src:17333)
GIVEN `the penalty is a financial penalty under section 1225D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225D(3) the penalty is payable to the Secretary of State` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is a financial penalty under section 1225D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A financial penalty under this section is payable to the Secretary of State"

-- src:17334 | (4) In sections 1225E to 1225G, references to a penalty are to a financial penalty under this section.
@ref s 1225D(4) "penalty" in sections 1225E to 1225G (src:17334)
GIVEN `the penalty is a financial penalty under section 1225D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225D(4) the reference to a penalty in sections 1225E to 1225G is to the penalty` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is a financial penalty under section 1225D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In sections 1225E to 1225G, references to a penalty are to a financial penalty under this section."

-- ---- s 1225E: Financial penalties: supplementary -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17336 | (1) Before imposing a penalty on a body, the Secretary of State must give the body a notice (a “notice of proposed penalty”)—
-- src:17337 | (a) stating that the Secretary of State proposes to impose a penalty and the amount of the penalty proposed,
-- src:17338 | (b) identifying the requirement or obligation in question and stating why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with, and
-- src:17339 | (c) specifying a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposed penalty.
@ref s 1225E(1) Notice of proposed penalty (src:17336-17339)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State gave the body a notice of proposed penalty before imposing the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the Secretary of State proposes to impose a penalty and the amount of the penalty proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice identifies the requirement or obligation in question and states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposed penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(1) the notice of proposed penalty was given and has the required content` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State gave the body a notice of proposed penalty before imposing the penalty`
       AND `the notice states that the Secretary of State proposes to impose a penalty and the amount of the penalty proposed`
       AND `the notice identifies the requirement or obligation in question and states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with`
       AND `the notice specifies a period within which the body may make written representations with respect to the proposed penalty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before imposing a penalty on a body, the Secretary of State must give the body a notice (a “notice of proposed penalty”)— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..."

-- src:17340 | (2) The period specified under subsection (1)(c)—
-- src:17341 | (a) must begin with the date on which the notice of proposed penalty is given to the body, and
-- src:17342 | (b) must not be less than 21 days.
@ref s 1225E(2) The period for representations (src:17340-17342)
GIVEN `the period begins with the date on which the notice of proposed penalty is given to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the length of the period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(2) the period specified under subsection (1)(c) is valid` MEANS
    IF `the period begins with the date on which the notice of proposed penalty is given to the body` AND `the length of the period in days` AT LEAST 21
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period specified under subsection (1)(c)— (a) must begin with the date on which the notice of proposed penalty is given to the body, and (b) must not be less than 21 days."

-- src:17343 | (3) Written representations made by the body before the end of the period specified under subsection (1)(c) must be considered by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1225E(3) Representations must be considered (src:17343)
GIVEN `the body made written representations before the end of the period specified under subsection (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considered them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(3) the Secretary of State has complied with the duty to consider the representations` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body made written representations before the end of the period specified under subsection (1)(c)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Written representations made by the body before the end of the period specified under subsection (1)(c) must be considered"
    ELSE IF `the Secretary of State considered them`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be considered by the Secretary of State"

-- src:17344 | (4) After considering any such representations or, in their absence, on the expiry of the period specified under subsection (1)(c), the Secretary of State must decide—
-- src:17345 | (a) whether to impose a penalty, and
-- src:17346 | (b) where the Secretary of State decides to do so, whether to reduce the proposed amount of the penalty.
@ref s 1225E(4) The decision whether to impose a penalty and whether to reduce it (src:17344-17346)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has considered any representations or, in their absence, the period specified under subsection (1)(c) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(4) the Secretary of State must now decide whether to impose a penalty and whether to reduce the proposed amount` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has considered any representations or, in their absence, the period specified under subsection (1)(c) has expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After considering any such representations or, in their absence, on the expiry of the period specified under subsection (1)(c), the Secretary of State must decide" (a time fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:17347 | (5) The Secretary of State must give notice of the decision (a “penalty decision notice”) to the body.
@ref s 1225E(5) Notice of the decision (src:17347)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decided whether to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(5) the Secretary of State has given notice of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decided whether to impose a penalty` AND `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must give notice of the decision (a “penalty decision notice”) to the body."

-- src:17348 | (6) Where the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty, the penalty decision notice must—
-- src:17349 | (a) state that the Secretary of State has imposed a penalty on the body and its amount,
-- src:17350 | (b) identify the requirement or obligation in question and state—
-- src:17351 | (i) why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with, or
-- src:17352 | (ii) where, by that time, the requirement is satisfied or the obligation has been complied with, why it appeared to the Secretary of State when giving the notice of proposed penalty that the requirement was not satisfied or the obligation had not been complied with, and
-- src:17353 | (c) specify a time by which the penalty is required to be paid.
@ref s 1225E(6) Content of the penalty decision notice (src:17348-17353)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the Secretary of State has imposed a penalty on the body and its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by that time the requirement is satisfied or the obligation has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states why it appeared to the Secretary of State when giving the notice of proposed penalty that the requirement was not satisfied or the obligation had not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a time by which the penalty is required to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(6) the penalty decision notice has the required content` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty`
    THEN (IF     `the notice states that the Secretary of State has imposed a penalty on the body and its amount`
             AND `the notice specifies a time by which the penalty is required to be paid`
             AND (IF `by that time the requirement is satisfied or the obligation has been complied with`
                  THEN `the notice states why it appeared to the Secretary of State when giving the notice of proposed penalty that the requirement was not satisfied or the obligation had not been complied with`
                  ELSE `the notice states why it appears to the Secretary of State that the requirement is not satisfied or the obligation has not been complied with`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the penalty decision notice must— (a) state that the Secretary of State has imposed a penalty on the body and its amount, (b) identify the requirement or obligation ... and state— (i) ... or (ii) ..., and (c) specify a time by which the penalty is required to be paid"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17354 | (7) The time specified under subsection (6)(c) must be at least 3 months after the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body.
@ref s 1225E(7) The time for payment (src:17354)
GIVEN `the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body` IS A DATE
      `the time specified for payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(7) the time specified for payment is valid` MEANS
    -- at least 3 months after the date on which the notice is given: the day three months on is allowed. `Date` rolls a day that does not exist
    -- in the later month (31 August plus 3 months is 31 November) forward into the next month: a fork, see the fork register.
    IF `the time specified for payment` AT LEAST `three months after the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The time specified under subsection (6)(c) must be at least 3 months after the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body."
    WHERE
        `three months after the notice` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body`) (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body` PLUS 3) (DATE_YEAR `the date on which the penalty decision notice is given to the body`)

-- src:17355 | (8) Where the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty, the Secretary of State must publish the penalty decision notice and must do so in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the penalty to the attention of persons likely to be affected.
@ref s 1225E(8) Publication of the penalty decision notice (src:17355)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State published the penalty decision notice in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the penalty to the attention of persons likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(8) the Secretary of State has published the penalty decision notice` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty` AND `the Secretary of State published the penalty decision notice in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate for bringing the penalty to the attention of persons likely to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Secretary of State decides to impose a penalty, the Secretary of State must publish the penalty decision notice"

-- src:17356 | (9) The Secretary of State may rescind a penalty imposed on a body under section 1225D and, where doing so, must—
-- src:17357 | (a) give the body notice of the rescission, and
-- src:17358 | (b) publish the notice in the same manner as the penalty decision notice was published.
@ref s 1225E(9) Rescission of a penalty (src:17356-17358)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State rescinds a penalty imposed on a body under section 1225D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the rescission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State published the notice in the same manner as the penalty decision notice was published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225E(9) the rescission of the penalty complies with subsection (9)` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State rescinds a penalty imposed on a body under section 1225D`
    THEN (IF `the Secretary of State gave the body notice of the rescission` AND `the Secretary of State published the notice in the same manner as the penalty decision notice was published`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where doing so, must— (a) give the body notice of the rescission, and (b) publish the notice in the same manner as the penalty decision notice was published"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may rescind a penalty imposed on a body under section 1225D and, where doing so, must"

-- ---- s 1225F: Appeals against financial penalties ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17361 | (2) The appeal grounds are—
-- src:17362 | (a) that, before the giving of the notice under section 1225E(1), the requirement in respect of which the penalty was imposed was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the penalty was imposed had been complied with;
-- src:17363 | (b) that, where the penalty was imposed in respect of a failure to comply with a direction under section 1225A, before the giving of the notice under section 1225B(6), the requirement in respect of which the direction was given was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the direction was given had been complied with;
-- src:17364 | (c) that any of the requirements of section 1225E have not been complied with in relation to the imposition of the penalty and the interests of the body have been substantially prejudiced by the non-compliance;
-- src:17365 | (d) that the amount of the penalty is unreasonable;
-- src:17366 | (e) that it was unreasonable of the Secretary of State to require the penalty imposed to be paid by the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5).
@ref s 1225F(2) The appeal grounds (src:17361-17366)
GIVEN `before the giving of the notice under section 1225E(1), the requirement in respect of which the penalty was imposed was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the penalty was imposed had been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty was imposed in respect of a failure to comply with a direction under section 1225A and, before the giving of the notice under section 1225B(6), the requirement in respect of which the direction was given was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the direction was given had been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the requirements of section 1225E have not been complied with in relation to the imposition of the penalty and the interests of the body have been substantially prejudiced by the non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the penalty is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was unreasonable of the Secretary of State to require the penalty imposed to be paid by the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(2) an appeal ground is made out` MEANS
    IF     `before the giving of the notice under section 1225E(1), the requirement in respect of which the penalty was imposed was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the penalty was imposed had been complied with`
        OR `the penalty was imposed in respect of a failure to comply with a direction under section 1225A and, before the giving of the notice under section 1225B(6), the requirement in respect of which the direction was given was satisfied or the obligation in respect of which the direction was given had been complied with`
        OR `any of the requirements of section 1225E have not been complied with in relation to the imposition of the penalty and the interests of the body have been substantially prejudiced by the non-compliance`
        OR `the amount of the penalty is unreasonable`
        OR `it was unreasonable of the Secretary of State to require the penalty imposed to be paid by the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appeal grounds are— (a) ... (e) ..." (a list closed by "are", read as the keel reads "are": a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17360 | (1) A body on which a penalty is imposed may appeal to the court on one or more of the appeal grounds.
@ref s 1225F(1) The right of appeal (src:17360)
GIVEN `a penalty is imposed on the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal ground is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(1) the body may appeal to the court` MEANS
    IF NOT `a penalty is imposed on the body`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A body on which a penalty is imposed may appeal"
    ELSE IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `an appeal ground is made out`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal is "on one or more of the appeal grounds"; whether the body may appeal on other grounds is not decided here

-- src:17367 | (3) An appeal under subsection (1) must be made within the period of 3 months beginning with the day on which the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty.
@ref s 1225F(3) The time for appealing (src:17367)
GIVEN `the day the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(3) the appeal is made in time` MEANS
    -- "within the period of 3 months beginning with the day": from that day up to, but not including, the same day three months on.
    IF     `the day the appeal is made` AT LEAST `the day the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty`
       AND `the day the appeal is made` LESS THAN `three months on`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal under subsection (1) must be made within the period of 3 months beginning with the day on which the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty." (a period fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHERE
        `three months on` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the day the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty` PLUS 3) (DATE_YEAR `the day the notice under section 1225E(5) is given to the body in respect of the penalty`)

DECLARE `s 1225F(4) step the court may take` IS ONE OF
    `s 1225F(4)(a) quash the penalty`
    `s 1225F(4)(b) substitute a penalty of such lesser amount as the court considers appropriate`
    `s 1225F(4)(c) substitute a later time for the time specified in the notice`

-- src:17368 | (4) On any such appeal, where the court considers it appropriate to do so in all the circumstances of the case and is satisfied of one or more of the appeal grounds, the court may—
-- src:17369 | (a) quash the penalty,
-- src:17370 | (b) substitute a penalty of such lesser amount as the court considers appropriate, or
-- src:17371 | (c) in the case of the appeal ground in subsection (2)(e), substitute a later time for the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5).
@ref s 1225F(4) What the court may do on an appeal (src:17368-17371)
GIVEN step IS A `s 1225F(4) step the court may take`
      `the court considers it appropriate to do so in all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied of one or more of the appeal grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal ground is the ground in subsection (2)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(4) the court may take the step` MEANS
    IF `the court considers it appropriate to do so in all the circumstances of the case` AND `the court is satisfied of one or more of the appeal grounds`
    THEN CONSIDER step
         WHEN `s 1225F(4)(a) quash the penalty` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1225F(4)(b) substitute a penalty of such lesser amount as the court considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1225F(4)(c) substitute a later time for the time specified in the notice` THEN
             IF `the appeal ground is the ground in subsection (2)(e)`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) in the case of the appeal ground in subsection (2)(e)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On any such appeal, where the court considers it appropriate to do so in all the circumstances of the case and is satisfied of one or more of the appeal grounds, the court may" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17372 | (5) Where the court substitutes a penalty of a lesser amount, it may require the payment of interest on the substituted penalty, accruing from the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5) or such later time as the court considers just and equitable.
@ref s 1225F(5) Interest on a substituted lesser penalty (src:17372)
GIVEN `the court substitutes a penalty of a lesser amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(5) the court may require the payment of interest on the substituted penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court substitutes a penalty of a lesser amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court substitutes a penalty of a lesser amount, it may require the payment of interest on the substituted penalty" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17373 | (6) Where the court substitutes a later time for the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5), it may require the payment of interest on the penalty, accruing from the substituted time or such later time as the court considers just and equitable.
@ref s 1225F(6) Interest where a later time is substituted (src:17373)
GIVEN `the court substitutes a later time for the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(6) the court may require the payment of interest on the penalty from the substituted time` MEANS
    IF `the court substitutes a later time for the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court substitutes a later time for the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5), it may require the payment of interest on the penalty" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17374 | (7) Where the court dismisses the appeal, it may require the payment of interest on the penalty, accruing from the time specified in the notice under section 1225E(5).
@ref s 1225F(7) Interest where the appeal is dismissed (src:17374)
GIVEN `the court dismisses the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(7) the court may require the payment of interest on the penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court dismisses the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court dismisses the appeal, it may require the payment of interest on the penalty" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17375 | (8) Where the court requires the payment of interest under this section, the interest is payable at such rate as the court considers just and equitable.
@ref s 1225F(8) The rate of interest (src:17375)
GIVEN `the court requires the payment of interest under section 1225F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(8) the interest is payable at such rate as the court considers just and equitable` MEANS
    IF `the court requires the payment of interest under section 1225F`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court requires the payment of interest under this section, the interest is payable at such rate as the court considers just and equitable." (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:17376 | (9) Except as provided by this section, the validity of a penalty is not to be questioned by any legal proceedings whatever.
@ref s 1225F(9) No other challenge to the validity of a penalty (src:17376)
GIVEN `the proceedings are an appeal provided for by section 1225F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225F(9) the validity of the penalty may be questioned in the legal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are an appeal provided for by section 1225F`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided by this section"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided by this section, the validity of a penalty is not to be questioned by any legal proceedings whatever."

DECLARE `s 1225F(10) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1225F(10) the High Court`
    `s 1225F(10) the Court of Session`

-- src:17377 | (10) In this section “ the court ” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 1225F(10) "the court" (src:17377)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1225F(10) court`
`s 1225F(10) the court is` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
    THEN `s 1225F(10) the Court of Session`
    ELSE `s 1225F(10) the High Court`

-- ---- s 1225G: Recovery of financial penalties ----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17379 | (1) If the whole or any part of a penalty is not paid by the time by which it is required to be paid, the unpaid balance from time to time carries interest at the rate for the time being specified in section 17 of the Judgments Act 1838 (c 110) (unless a different rate is specified by the court under section 1225F(8)).
@ref s 1225G(1) Interest on an unpaid penalty (src:17379)
GIVEN `the whole or any part of the penalty is not paid by the time by which it is required to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a different rate is specified by the court under section 1225F(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225G(1) the unpaid balance carries interest at the rate specified in section 17 of the Judgments Act 1838` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the whole or any part of the penalty is not paid by the time by which it is required to be paid` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the whole or any part of a penalty is not paid by the time by which it is required to be paid"
        IF `a different rate is specified by the court under section 1225F(8)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(unless a different rate is specified by the court under section 1225F(8))"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:17380 | (2) If an appeal is made under section 1225F in relation to a penalty, the penalty is not required to be paid until the appeal has been determined or withdrawn.
@ref s 1225G(2) No payment while an appeal is pending (src:17380)
GIVEN `an appeal is made under section 1225F in relation to the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been determined or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225G(2) the penalty cannot yet be required to be paid` MEANS
    -- the "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE before the appeal is determined or withdrawn, JUST FALSE after it
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an appeal is made under section 1225F in relation to the penalty` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal is made under section 1225F in relation to a penalty"
        IF `the appeal has been determined or withdrawn` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the penalty is not required to be paid until the appeal has been determined or withdrawn"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:17381 | (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the court from specifying that interest is to accrue from an earlier date under section 1225F.
@ref s 1225G(3) Interest from an earlier date (src:17381)
GIVEN `the court specifies that interest is to accrue from an earlier date under section 1225F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225G(3) subsection (2) prevents the court from specifying that interest is to accrue from an earlier date` MEANS
    IF `the court specifies that interest is to accrue from an earlier date under section 1225F`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not prevent the court from specifying that interest is to accrue from an earlier date under section 1225F."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of an earlier date specified under section 1225F

-- src:17382 | (4) Where a penalty, or any portion of it, has not been paid by the time when it is required to be paid and—
-- src:17383 | (a) no appeal relating to the penalty has been made under section 1225F during the period within which such an appeal can be made, or
-- src:17384 | (b) an appeal has been made under that section and has been determined or withdrawn,
-- src:17385 | the Secretary of State may recover from the body, as a debt due to the Secretary of State, any of the penalty and any interest which has not been paid.
@ref s 1225G(4) Recovery as a debt (src:17382-17385)
GIVEN `the penalty, or a portion of it, has not been paid by the time when it is required to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no appeal relating to the penalty has been made under section 1225F during the period within which such an appeal can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal has been made under section 1225F and has been determined or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1225G(4) the Secretary of State may recover the unpaid penalty and interest from the body as a debt` MEANS
    IF     `the penalty, or a portion of it, has not been paid by the time when it is required to be paid`
       AND (   `no appeal relating to the penalty has been made under section 1225F during the period within which such an appeal can be made`
            OR `an appeal has been made under section 1225F and has been determined or withdrawn`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a penalty, or any portion of it, has not been paid by the time when it is required to be paid and— (a) ... or (b) ..., the Secretary of State may recover" (a "where" that fails: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
